  "description": "This is an application for change of use \n\nFROM: C3 residential  (or C4 HMO if the property is classed as this through previous HMO licences obtained prior to the introduction of the mandatory planning application in Nov 2024).\n\nTO: Sui Generis (HMO) planning application as mandated by the HMO licence conditions. HMO has 7+ occupants.\n\nThe Council has approved the latest application for a licence for the house in multiple occupation known as 2, Allan Way, London, W3 0PN on 14 March 2025\nOne of the conditions was: \n\nPlanning permission and HMO licensing are two different and distinct legal requirements. Planning\npermission must usually be obtained before the property is occupied as an HMO, however, we will\nbe granting you 12 months to allow you the opportunity to regularise and to meet the requirements\nof the Planning department by applying for Change of Use permission, either C4 (HMO) or Sui\nGeneris (HMO). \n\nProperty has been a HMO for over 10 years. \n\nLatest HMO licence was approved in March 2025 expiring in February 2026 in order to provide time to obtain newly introduced planning permission requirement (November 2024) in order to apply for a 5 year licence.\n\nThe licence is attached.\n\nAs this requirement was only introduced in November 2024 at short notice, both the planning and licensing departments have been approached for guidance multiple times. Neither have provided any guidance. Therefore this form and documents have been submitted to the best of knowledge and ability. A planning call back was requested on 17 November 2025. As of the date this application has been submitted, the call back has not taken place. \n\nThe dates below are the dates of commencement of the latest HMO licence - applied for in December 2023; approved in March 2025.\n",
